data: {"type":"response.function_call_arguments.done","sequence_number":1860,"item_id":"fc_0d700e9f47bf6b53016adb32af6ce481919ccff189579ebdc3","output_index":1,"arguments":"{\"artifact_json\":\"{\\\"base_input\\\":\\\"prior-candidate.json\\\",\\\"patches\\\":[{\\\"op\\\":\\\"replace\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"/graph/inferences/0/locals/12/symbol\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"b_i\\\"},{\\\"op\\\":\\\"replace\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"/graph/inferences/0/locals/12/type\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"image of a e_i in M_R/pM_R, then extended to M tensor_Z K\\\"},{\\\"op\\\":\\\"replace\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"/graph/inferences/0/locals/12/start\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"S004\\\"},{\\\"op\\\":\\\"replace\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"/graph/inferences/0/locals/12/end\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"S005\\\"},{\\\"op\\\":\\\"replace\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"/graph/inferences/0/locals/12/declaration\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"For each 0<=i<=lambda define b_i as the image of a e_i under M_R -> M_R/pM_R and then under the canonical scalar-extension identification (M_R/pM_R) tensor_F_p K = M tensor_Z K.\\\"},{\\\"op\\\":\\\"replace\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"/graph/inferences/0/locals/12/from_local\\\",\\\"value\\\":[\\\"F001\\\"]},{\\\"op\\\":\\\"replace\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"/graph/inferences/0/locals/12/objects\\\",\\\"value\\\":[\\\"a\\\",\\\"e_i\\\",\\\"M_R\\\",\\\"F_p\\\",\\\"K\\\",\\\"M\\\"]},{\\\"op\\\":\\\"replace\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"/graph/inferences/0/locals/13/symbol\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"F_p\\\"},{\\\"op\\\":\\\"replace\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"/graph/inferences/0/locals/13/type\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"prime subfield of K\\\"},{\\\"op\\\":\\\"replace\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"/graph/inferences/0/locals/13/scope\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"R001\\\"},{\\\"op\\\":\\\"replace\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"/graph/inferences/0/locals/13/start\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"S004\\\"},{\\\"op\\\":\\\"replace\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"/graph/inferences/0/locals/13/end\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"S005\\\"},{\\\"op\\\":\\\"replace\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"/graph/inferences/0/locals/13/kind\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"definition\\\"},{\\\"op\\\":\\\"replace\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"/graph/inferences/0/locals/13/declaration\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"Let F_p be the prime subfield of K, canonically isomorphic to Z/pZ.\\\"},{\\\"op\\\":\\\"replace\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"/graph/inferences/0/locals/13/from_inputs\\\",\\\"value\\\":[\\\"H001\\\",\\\"H002\\\"]},{\\\"op\\\":\\\"replace\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"/graph/inferences/0/locals/13/from_local\\\",\\\"value\\\":[]},{\\\"op\\\":\\\"replace\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"/graph/inferences/0/locals/13/objects\\\",\\\"value\\\":[\\\"p\\\",\\\"K\\\"]},{\\\"op\\\":\\\"replace\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"/graph/inferences/0/locals/14/symbol\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"W\\\"},{\\\"op\\\":\\\"replace\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"/graph/inferences/0/locals/14/type\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"invariant K-subspace\\\"},{\\\"op\\\":\\\"replace\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"/graph/inferences/0/locals/14/scope\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"R001\\\"},{\\\"op\\\":\\\"replace\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"/graph/inferences/0/locals/14/start\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"S005\\\"},{\\\"op\\\":\\\"replace\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"/graph/inferences/0/locals/14/end\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"S005\\\"},{\\\"op\\\":\\\"replace\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"/graph/inferences/0/locals/14/kind\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"arbitrary\\\"},{\\\"op\\\":\\\"replace\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"/graph/inferences/0/locals/14/declaration\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"Let W be any K-subspace invariant under x,y,h.\\\"},{\\\"op\\\":\\\"replace\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"/graph/inferences/0/locals/14/from_inputs\\\",\\\"value\\\":[\\\"H002\\\",\\\"H003\\\",\\\"H004\\\"]},{\\\"op\\\":\\\"replace\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"/graph/inferences/0/locals/14/from_local\\\",\\\"value\\\":[]},{\\\"op\\\":\\\"replace\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"/graph/inferences/0/locals/14/objects\\\",\\\"value\\\":[\\\"K\\\",\\\"M\\\",\\\"x\\\",\\\"y\\\",\\\"h\\\"]},{\\\"op\\\":\\\"replace\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"/graph/inferences/0/locals/15/symbol\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"r\\\"},{\\\"op\\\":\\\"replace\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"/graph/inferences/0/locals/15/type\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"integer with 0<=r<=lambda\\\"},{\\\"op\\\":\\\"replace\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"/graph/inferences/0/locals/15/scope\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"R001\\\"},{\\\"op\\\":\\\"replace\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"/graph/inferences/0/locals/15/start\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"S005\\\"},{\\\"op\\\":\\\"replace\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"/graph/inferences/0/locals/15/end\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"S005\\\"},{\\\"op\\\":\\\"replace\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"/graph/inferences/0/locals/15/kind\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"arbitrary\\\"},{\\\"op\\\":\\\"replace\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"/graph/inferences/0/locals/15/declaration\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"Fix arbitrary r with 0<=r<=lambda.\\\"},{\\\"op\\\":\\\"replace\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"/graph/inferences/0/locals/15/from_inputs\\\",\\\"value\\\":[\\\"H003\\\"]},{\\\"op\\\":\\\"replace\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"/graph/inferences/0/locals/15/from_local\\\",\\\"value\\\":[]},{\\\"op\\\":\\\"replace\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"/graph/inferences/0/locals/15/objects\\\",\\\"value\\\":[\\\"lambda\\\"]},{\\\"op\\\":\\\"replace\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"/graph/inferences/0/argument/3/text\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"On the R-basis a e_0,...,a e_lambda established above, x(ae_i)=(lambda-i+1)ae_(i-1), y(ae_i)=(i+1)ae_(i+1), and h(ae_i)=(lambda-2i)ae_i, with out-of-range terms zero. Let F_p be the prime subfield of K. The images of a e_i form an F_p-basis of M_R/pM_R because a e_i are an R-basis of M_R and R/pR=F_p. The natural map M_R/pM_R -> M tensor_Z F_p is an isomorphism: localizing M at integers prime to p does not change its reduction modulo p; concretely, denominators prime to p become invertible mod p. Thus this same reduced basis is a basis of M tensor_Z F_p. Extending scalars along F_p -> K gives the K-basis b_0,...,b_lambda of M tensor_Z K, where b_i denotes the image of a e_i under these quotient and scalar-extension maps. These maps carry each integral action matrix to its reduction and then to K, so the reduced action on b_i is x b_i=(lambda-i+1)b_(i-1), y b_i=(i+1)b_(i+1), h b_i=(lambda-2i)b_i (out-of-range terms zero). This is the explicit representation correspondence; the characteristic-zero e_i themselves are not being used as vectors in M tensor_Z K.\\\"},{\\\"op\\\":\\\"replace\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"/graph/inferences/0/argument/3/objects\\\",\\\"value\\\":[\\\"a\\\",\\\"e_i\\\",\\\"x\\\",\\\"y\\\",\\\"h\\\",\\\"lambda\\\",\\\"M_R\\\",\\\"p\\\",\\\"F_p\\\",\\\"K\\\",\\\"M\\\",\\\"L(K)\\\",\\\"b_i\\\"]},{\\\"op\\\":\\\"replace\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"/graph/inferences/0/argument/4/text\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"For 0<=r<=lambda<p, r! is invertible modulo p, so the reductions of X_r and Y_r are scalar multiples of the corresponding powers of x and y on M tensor_Z K. The characteristic-zero identities defining E_i,j preserve M_R and their matrices in the R-basis a e_t are the usual matrix-unit matrices; therefore their reductions, followed by scalar extension to K, are the matrix units in the explicitly defined basis b_0,...,b_lambda. Equivalently, the identities from S002 persist under these maps; every coefficient binom(lambda,j) is nonzero modulo p (since 0<=j<=lambda<p), hence a unit in F_p and K. Thus any K-subspace W invariant under x and y is invariant under each reduced E_i,j. Write a nonzero w in W as w=sum_i c_i b_i and choose i with c_i nonzero. For every j, the reduced E_j,i sends w to c_i b_j, so b_j belongs to W because c_i is invertible in K. Hence W is the whole module. Its basis has lambda+1 vectors, a positive integer, so it is nonzero. This proves irreducibility, including lambda=0 and p=2.\\\"},{\\\"op\\\":\\\"replace\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"/graph/inferences/0/argument/4/objects\\\",\\\"value\\\":[\\\"r\\\",\\\"lambda\\\",\\\"p\\\",\\\"X_r\\\",\\\"Y_r\\\",\\\"x\\\",\\\"y\\\",\\\"E_i,j\\\",\\\"K\\\",\\\"W\\\",\\\"b_i\\\"]}]}\" }"}

